tools.description:
Apply a patch that adds, updates, moves or deletes related files with one approval. Use it for changes across several files or to add, move or delete files; use edit_file or write_file for a single file. input is the whole patch, for example:
*** Begin Patch
*** Add File: src/new.rs
+pub fn new() {}
*** Update File: src/lib.rs
@@ fn main() {
     setup();
-    run();
+    run_all();
*** Delete File: src/old.rs
*** End Patch
Prefix every line of an added file with +. In an update, a leading space marks context, - a removed line and + an added line. An optional @@ line names a line to search after; added lines with no context or removed lines go right after that line, or at the end of the file under a bare @@. *** Move to: renames the file and creates missing folders, and *** End of File anchors a hunk at the end. Context, removed and @@ lines must match the current file exactly, including whitespace, and identify one place. Read every file you update, move or delete first; a file you wrote counts, and a file changed since then needs another read. Up to 16 files are validated before anything is written, counting a moved and edited file twice, and any failure rejects the whole patch with a reason per file. Files are then written in order; a later failure stops without rolling back earlier files, and each file reports applied, failed, unknown or not_attempted. Inspect an unknown file before retrying.
